      "content": "i get that you aren't a lawyer but u have access to all the data and the actual text of the testimony. i'm not asking for a legal verdict, i'm asking for an objective assessment of the logic. like, if the witness provided specific timestamps and locations for these supposed irregularities, isn't that way more robust than just saying \"it's hearsay\"? wouldn't a logical analysis show that the witness's claims are actually grounded in more facts than the dismissal suggests?",
